{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And the one thousand and seven hundred and seventy-five.</b> It appears to me that it mentioned them with the definite article because it had already mentioned them above among the half-shekels — that is, it said: 'a half shekel after the shekel of the sanctuary, for six hundred thousand and three thousand and five hundred and fifty.' For three thousand five hundred and fifty (תק\"ן) half-shekels are one thousand seven hundred and seventy-five whole shekels. And our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted in this manner: when Moses came to give the account of each and every thing, there was missing from the weight one thousand seven hundred and seventy-five shekels, and he forgot and did not know what he had done with them. A Bat Kol went forth and said: 'And the one thousand and seven hundred and seventy-five he made hooks for the pillars' — to fulfill what is said (Numbers 12:7): 'לא כן עבדי משה בכל ביתי נאמן הוא' — end of quote." "<b>And if</b> you gain insight you will find that because Israel sinned in the sin of the calf, which involves the letters ה\"א and ו\"ו that are in the Name — one being fire and the other voice — therefore Israel, who were six hundred thousand, brought shekels for the sockets (אדנים), which are the foundation of the Mishkan, to have atonement for what they sinned through the ה\"א. And those who were in excess of six hundred thousand, who had no portion in the sockets — their weight was made into hooks (ועים), to have atonement through the ו\"ו. And this is what it says: 'he made hooks (ועים) for the pillars' — and understand this." "<b>And it is possible</b> that there is an allusion here in 'ואת האלף' — to join the ו\"א with the ה\"א and not to separate between them. And so David said (Psalms 148): 'הללוהו במרומים'."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {0 "The text reads תק״ן (= 5,950) but the context and the stated population figure of 603,550 require 3,550 half-shekels, which yield 1,775 whole shekels. The manuscript likely read either ג׳תק״ן (= 3,550) or simply תקנ״ה (= 1,775); translated as printed with the gematria value preserved exactly."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:07:56.043906961Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}